    "For JS-rendered targets, drive Playwright or Puppeteer with resource blocking (disable images/fonts) to cut per-page load time and bandwidth, and capture the rendered DOM rather than the network responses directly.",
    "Write per-template extractors (CSS/XPath selectors or a vision-based layout model) that map raw markup to a structured schema (e.g. listing → {price, title, seller, location, timestamp}).",
    "Route all requests through a rotating proxy/unblocking layer (see web_proxy) and randomize TLS fingerprints, header order and viewport to resemble organic browser traffic.",
    "Throttle per-domain concurrency and add randomized jitter between requests; treat each target's observed rate-limit threshold as a budget to stay under, not a wall to push against.",
    "Validate extracted records against a schema and sanity bounds (price > 0, date parses, required fields non-null) before they enter the pipeline, routing failures to a manual-repair queue.",
    "Version selectors per site and run a canary job hourly against a small sample to detect template drift before it silently corrupts the full-scale run.",
