    "For residential proxy networks, recruit exit nodes through a disclosed, consented SDK bundled in free apps or VPN products, compensating users or offering a free-tier service in exchange for bandwidth sharing.",
    "Build a proxy-management layer that tracks per-IP health (success rate, block rate, response-time distribution) and automatically retires IPs showing block patterns.",
    "Pair each proxy with a matching browser/TLS fingerprint profile (consistent User-Agent, header order, TLS cipher suite, canvas/WebGL fingerprint) so IP geography and client fingerprint don't contradict each other.",
    "Implement session-stickiness options (same IP across a multi-request session) versus per-request rotation, exposing both as configurable modes since different scraping tasks need different consistency.",
    "Geotarget IP selection to country/city/ASN level so customers can request a specific vantage point (needed for geo-restricted or localized content).",
    "Rate-limit per-target usage across the whole pool, not just per IP, so no single customer's traffic pattern (even spread across thousands of IPs) looks anomalous to the target.",
    "Expose the pool through a simple proxy or unblocker API (HTTP/SOCKS endpoint, or a full 'scraping browser' that handles rendering and CAPTCHA-solving behind the scenes).",
    "Monitor and respond to abuse complaints and legal notices about pool IPs being used for unwanted traffic, since residential pool operators bear reputational and partnership risk from misuse.",
