    "Parse each format into a normalized schema (entity ID, name, status, address, dates), handling the registry's own ID scheme (company number, CIK, LEI) as the durable join key across releases.",
    "Diff each new bulk release against the previous one to produce a change feed (new entities, status changes, dissolutions) rather than reprocessing the full dataset downstream every cycle.",
    "Retain every historical snapshot, not just the latest, since registries routinely remove or amend records and historical state is often the analytically valuable part.",
    "Monitor for registry-side format or schema changes (new fields, encoding changes) by diffing the file header/schema on each ingest before running the full parse.",
