    "Direct cost is low to near-zero since most bulk products are free government publications; cost is in pipeline engineering and ongoing parsing maintenance, not acquisition.",
    "Monetized indirectly as the free raw-material layer underneath paid aggregation products (corporate-ownership platforms, screening tools) that add entity resolution and enrichment.",
    "Moat is near-zero at the raw-data layer since anyone can download the same files; defensibility shifts entirely to downstream normalization, cross-registry entity resolution and enrichment.",
    "Freshness lag is inherent (monthly/quarterly publishing cycles), so this method is unsuitable for near-real-time use cases without supplementing with live-query APIs for specific lookups.",
    "Build-vs-buy almost always favors building the ingestion pipeline directly, since the data is free; the buy decision is really about the downstream entity-resolution layer.",
